Sure! To update the `version` property of your `packageInfo` object only when the new value differs (or when the property doesn’t exist yet), you can use the `vOe` helper.  
Below is a quick example of how you’d call it. I’ll need the current contents of `packageInfo` so that the function can compare the existing value with the new one. If you can paste the current object (or its JSON representation) here, I’ll plug it into the call for you.

```javascript
// Example current object (replace this with your actual packageInfo)
const currentPackageInfo = {
  name: "my-app",
  version: "1.0.0",
  description: "A sample app"
};

// Call the helper to update the version
functions.vOe({
  r: JSON.stringify(currentPackageInfo), // the object as a string
  e: "version",                          // property to update
  t: "1.2.3"                             // new value
});
```

